menu "Station: RTCM fan-out hub"

    config RTCM_HUB_RING_KB
        int "Shared frame ring size (KB, PSRAM)"
        range 32 2048
        default 256
        help
            One ring holds every RTCM3 frame received from the GNSS link; all
            consumers (casters, live view, future local server/logger) read
            from it with their own cursor. 256 KB holds about two minutes of
            a full MSM7 set at 1 Hz.

    config RTCM_HUB_MAX_CONSUMERS
        int "Maximum simultaneous consumers"
        range 2 24
        default 12
        help
            Caster slots plus local consumers (web live view, local TCP server,
            SD logger).

    config RTCM_HUB_MAX_LAG_MS
        int "Default slow-consumer lag limit (ms)"
        range 500 60000
        default 3000
        help
            A consumer whose oldest unread frame is older than its limit
            drops whole oldest epochs (finishing one already partly sent)
            until it is back under the limit; the dropped frames count as
            data loss for that consumer. Corrections are only useful while
            fresh. This is the default; the Onocoy slot sets 1000 ms.

    config RTCM_HUB_BURST_GAP_MS
        int "Gap that starts a new epoch while an MSM epoch is open (ms)"
        range 100 500
        default 250
        help
            Fallback epoch rule for a lost terminating MSM: a frame arriving
            this long after the previous one starts a new epoch while the
            current epoch holds an MSM not yet marked as its last.

endmenu
